         <listBibl>

            <bibl xml:id="bibl_1"><author key="mlgbAuthor_3606">Vitas patrum. Collections with this
                  common title invariably begin with Rufinus's translation (often ascribed to
                  Jerome) of the Historia monachorum in Aegypto (PL 21. 387—462; ed. E.
                  Schulz-Flügel [Berlin 1990]), and then go on to include other Lives and
                  apophthegmata of the type collected and published by H. Rosweyde and reprinted in
                  PL vols. 73—4. Jerome's Lives of St Paul the Hermit, St Hilarion, and St Malchus
                  (CPL 617—19) also make a frequent appearance. [See also Historia monachorum in
                  Aegypto; Jerome, Liber adhortationum sanctorum patrum.] </author><title
                  key="mlgbWork_3606_1"/></bibl>
